answer:
To determine the length of the fourth episode, follow these steps:

1. **Calculate the total duration of the first three episodes:**

   \[
   \begin{align*}
   \text{First episode} &= 58 \text{ minutes} \\
   \text{Second episode} &= 62 \text{ minutes} \\
   \text{Third episode} &= 65 \text{ minutes} \\
   \text{Total for first three episodes} &= 58 + 62 + 65 = 185 \text{ minutes}
   \end{align*}
   \]

2. **Convert the total duration of all four episodes from hours to minutes:**

   \[
   4 \text{ hours} = 4 \times 60 = 240 \text{ minutes}
   \]

3. **Determine the length of the fourth episode:**

   \[
   \begin{align*}
   \text{Total duration of four episodes} &= 240 \text{ minutes} \\
   \text{Total duration of first three episodes} &= 185 \text{ minutes} \\
   \text{Length of fourth episode} &= 240 - 185 = 55 \text{ minutes}
   \end{align*}
   \]

**Final Answer:**

\[
\boxed{55 \text{ minutes}}
\]

